{"id": "1.2-00020", "case_id": "github_lawrie_fpga_pio_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "github/lawrie/fpga_pio", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00020&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (20 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: src/pio.v, src/machine.v, src/decoder.v, src/divider.v, src/pc.v, src/scratch.v, src/fifo.v, src/isr.v and 1 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00020&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>9 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00020&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Fsrc%2Fdecoder.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed frozen testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>10 frozen testpoints:</strong> sim/copybit.v, sim/exec.v, sim/i2s.v, sim/pwm.v, sim/square.v, sim/stepper.v, sim/tb.v, sim/uart_rx.v, and 2 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00020&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00020&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># FPGA programmable-I/O project\nImplement the complete9-module PIO project described by the original README, with pio as its integration top. This is the pinned incomplete FPGA recreation, using its documented custom host-control interface; full Raspberry Pi RP2040 peripheral/register compatibility is not claimed. Keep NUM_MACHINES=4, matching its fixed four-machine status/mindex ports. The current examples exercise machine0.\n\nCurator interface and scope clarification from pinned RTL:\n- Rising clk and synchronous active-high reset. Load program/configuration before enable. Shared instruction RAM has32 words of16 bits; action1 writes din[15:0] at index. Each machine has X/Y scratch registers, ISR/OSR, independent TX/RX FIFO and program counter.\n- Host action0 reports version0x01000000 in dout;2 writes execution configuration for mindex,3 pops its RX FIFO to dout,4 pushes din to TX FIFO,5 configures GPIO groups,6 writes enable/restart/divider-restart masks,7 writes16.8 fixed-point divider,9 executes din[15:0] immediately even while disabled,10 sets shifts/autopush/autopull. Action8 is reserved/unimplemented. Hold din through the following control cycle for PUSH/immediate data, whose strobes are registered.\n- Action2 fields: status threshold[3:0], status source[4], wrap target[11:7], program end[16:12], sticky output[17], inline output enable[18], output-enable source[23:19], JMP pin[28:24], side-set direction[29], optional side-set flag[30], execution stall[31]. Some stored compatibility fields are not functionally implemented; do not claim untested full RP2040 behavior.\n- Action5 fields: OUT base[4:0], SET base[9:5], side-set base[14:10], IN base[19:15], OUT count[25:20], SET count[28:26], side-set count[31:29]. Action6 uses enable[3:0], restart[7:4], divider-restart[11:8]. Action7 stores24-bit divider and enables division only for values&gt;=0x200; action10 stores autopush16,autopull17,input direction18,output direction19, ISR threshold[24:20],OSR threshold[29:25]. Initialize required groups before running.\n- Instruction opcode[15:13]:0 JMP,1 WAIT,2 IN,3 OUT,4 PUSH/PULL,5 MOV,6 IRQ,7 SET. Operand1[7:5] and operand2[4:0] select condition/source/destination/immediate or bit count; instruction[12:8] is shared by delay and side-set fields. Zero shift count denotes32. JMP supports unconditional, X/Y zero and decrement conditions, X!=Y, selected GPIO and OSR-not-empty. SET selects pins/X/Y/pin directions; MOV selects pins/X/Y/null/status/ISR/OSR with identity/invert/bit reversal. IN/OUT shift configured directions and FIFO thresholds; PULL block waits for TX data, noblock substitutes X; PUSH block waits for space. Side-set and delay execute with the instruction, including documented stalled side-set behavior.\n- The selected documented programs require exact cycle timing: fractional divider2.5 alternates2/3 host-clock phases, delay1 doubles each SET duration, UART uses8N1 frames, stepper emits packed nibbles, I2S sends16-bit left/right channels and WS2812 distinguishes0/1 pulse widths. Original assembly/program files are supplied as specification examples; implement programmable behavior, not a fixed waveform generator.\n- GPIO updates are registered; when machines change the same output on one edge, the highest machine index wins. Reset clears enable/configuration/output state; instruction RAM must be loaded by host. IRQ0/IRQ1, unrestricted multi-machine interactions, and unsupported host compatibility fields are outside the qualified envelope; upstream leaves the two IRQ top outputs undriven.\n- Ten usable original program benches form ten points. The original SPI receive bench fails unchanged reference and is retained as an explicit excluded exception in testbench_inventory.json; it is not a required passing behavior. The copybit bench observes the first9 of10 queued words because the last lies beyond its original finish time. This is a documented observation limit, not another testpoint.\n\nSimulation I/O, delays, force/release, final blocks and external includes are forbidden. Constant elaboration functions ($clog2, $unsigned, $signed, $bits) and synthesizable storage initialization are permitted. Save all RTL under the exact required paths; only those files are collected.\n\nCompile this original Verilog project as Verilog2005 (-g2005); its source uses null as an ordinary identifier, which is reserved in SystemVerilog.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/0e6e83a78499999a1faba57ae0eca04b7e5bcd3d9e8fb8e1f7043c6a60350fd2.txt", "size": 23209, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/9379564162e044e31602be3094e35aa3e6db065b6118a330f0b79ef42b775c9b.txt", "size": 5316, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/direct_adapter.json", "url": "assets/18a544480bd73d43a3979590f84e7e6f2478ba0bb3e5bf6be3b16d290e541727.txt", "size": 639, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/decoder.v", "url": "assets/2f48a4cdfba80cb9168bf913990fbb07fa97effa06a4469c711f97c1f02e350c.txt", "size": 714, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/divider.v", "url": "assets/5b8232eeb43a236e8d91fa7f125f749ee78e44332d629dc4d7e590c0b35a9b89.txt", "size": 789, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/fifo.v", "url": "assets/b0ff70bce9211348fba752afb6216763884afb4271c87031993a8e0685648b6d.txt", "size": 1007, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/isr.v", "url": "assets/5f095b512d3dcde035bcf45a4cd9e13134cb3751db642a001c5e9851f1658229.txt", "size": 1280, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/machine.v", "url": "assets/09b6582b587044407d29260b670822043fd19e873e671cbedf99eeae9913e34f.txt", "size": 16036, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/src/osr.v"